       A "use VERSION" declaration has many implicit effects on the
       surrounding scope, such as strict and feature flags, or importing
       builtin functions. Once you have a "use VERSION" statement in scope,
       another "use VERSION" statement with a different version is now
       deprecated since Perl 5.39.8, due to the increasing complexity of
       swapping from one prevailing version to another.

       Category: "deprecated::subsequent_use_version"

